WEBVTT

02:41.826 --> 02:45.537
[ Rhythmic Droning ]

03:37.799 --> 03:40.050
[ Rattling ]

04:05.118 --> 04:07.369
[ Humming ]

04:11.624 --> 04:15.377
[ Electronic Chittering ]

04:16.879 --> 04:19.423
[ Clacking ]

04:31.394 --> 04:35.647
[ Distorted Computer Noises ]

04:35.732 --> 04:38.108
[ Noises Stop ]

06:37.311 --> 06:41.189
[ Chattering, Indistinct ]

06:49.782 --> 06:54.703
The food is terrible.
Worst shit
I've ever seen, man.

06:54.787 --> 06:57.247
[ Parker ]
What you say?
You got any biscuits over there?

06:57.331 --> 06:59.666
[ Ripley ]
I keep seeing corn bread.

07:02.420 --> 07:04.880
- I am cold.
- Still with us, Brett?

07:04.964 --> 07:09.342
- Right.
- Oh, I feel dead.

07:09.427 --> 07:12.304
Anybody ever tell you
you look dead, man?

07:14.724 --> 07:17.225
[ Mouthing Words ]
[ Parker ]
Oh, yeah, right.

07:17.310 --> 07:19.394
Now, I just
forgot something, man.

07:19.478 --> 07:21.438
Before we dock,

07:21.522 --> 07:23.523
I think we oughta discuss
the bonus situation.

07:23.649 --> 07:25.650
Right.
Brett and I,
we think we oughta-

07:25.735 --> 07:28.111
- We deserve full shares, right, baby?
- You see, Mr. Parker and I...

07:28.196 --> 07:31.823
feel that the bonus situation
has never been on
an equitable level.

07:31.908 --> 07:35.160
Well, you'll get
what you're contracted for
like everybody else.

07:35.286 --> 07:37.621
Yes, but everybody else
gets more than us.
[ Monitor Beeping ]

07:37.705 --> 07:39.873
Dallas, Mother
wants to talk to you.

07:39.957 --> 07:43.376
Huh? Yeah, I saw it.
Yellow light's
for my eyes only.

07:44.795 --> 07:46.546
Okay, get dressed, huh?

07:46.672 --> 07:50.091
Parker, come on.
Can I finish my coffee?
Thank you.

07:50.176 --> 07:52.636
It's the only thing
good on this ship.

07:53.888 --> 07:56.264
[ Chattering Continues ]

08:04.690 --> 08:07.609
[ Buzzes ]
[ Beeping ]

08:12.865 --> 08:15.867
[ Clacking ]
[ Electronic Chittering ]

08:39.767 --> 08:42.477
[ Dallas ]
Morning, Mother.

08:48.109 --> 08:50.068
[ Beeping, Whirring ]

09:08.587 --> 09:11.965
[ Voice Over Radio, Indistinct ]

09:12.049 --> 09:15.260
- Right.
- Okay.

09:15.344 --> 09:17.679
Plug us in.

09:18.889 --> 09:20.849
Thank you.

09:24.270 --> 09:27.605
- Where's Earth?
- You should know.

09:27.690 --> 09:30.859
It's not our system.

09:30.943 --> 09:31.484
Scan.

09:34.905 --> 09:37.907
[ Sighs ]
I can't believe this.

09:37.992 --> 09:41.244
Contact Traffic Control.

09:41.328 --> 09:45.707
[ Ripley ] This is
commercial towing vehicle
Nostromo out of the Solomons.

09:45.791 --> 09:49.836
Registration number:
1-8-0-niner-2-4-6-0-niner.

09:49.920 --> 09:54.507
Calling Antarctica
Traffic Control.
Can you read me? Over.

09:54.592 --> 09:57.844
Commercial towing vehicle
Nostromo out of the Solomons,

09:57.928 --> 09:59.929
registration number-

10:04.477 --> 10:06.978
Nothing.
[ Kane ]
Keep trying.

10:07.063 --> 10:11.191
Calling Antarctica
Traffic Control. Do you
read me, Antarctica? Over.

10:11.317 --> 10:15.820
I found it.
Just short of Zeta II Reticuli.
[ Ripley Chattering On Radio ]

10:15.946 --> 10:21.409
We haven't reached
the outer rim yet.
That's hard to believe.

10:21.494 --> 10:25.538
[ Lambert ]
What the hell
are we doing out here?

10:25.623 --> 10:28.374
I don't know.
What the hell are you talking about?

10:28.459 --> 10:31.836
- That's not our system.
- I know that.

10:31.962 --> 10:36.049
[ Loud Rumbling ]
[ Parker ] Do you ever notice
how they never come down here?

10:36.133 --> 10:38.259
I mean, this is where
the work is, right?

10:38.344 --> 10:41.012
Well, it's the same damn reason
we get a half share
to their one.

10:41.097 --> 10:43.139
Our time is their time.
That's the way they see it.

10:43.265 --> 10:45.183
No, but- Listen, man.
Same old shit, man.

10:45.267 --> 10:47.393
I think I know why they
don't come down here.

10:47.478 --> 10:49.979
It's because of you.
You don't have no personality.

10:51.982 --> 10:54.776
Wonder what they want now.
What's going on down here?

10:57.446 --> 11:00.532
Um, you happen to be
in my seat. Can I have it?
Yes, of course.

11:00.658 --> 11:03.576
Thank you.
I'm sorry.

11:03.661 --> 11:05.829
[ Wiping ]

11:08.165 --> 11:10.166
[ Parker ]
What's happenin' now, baby?

11:12.002 --> 11:16.214
Well, some of you
may have figured out
we're not home yet.

11:16.298 --> 11:18.675
- We're only halfway there.
- What?

11:18.759 --> 11:22.137
Mother's interrupted
the course of our journey.

11:22.221 --> 11:24.139
Why?
Yeah.

11:24.223 --> 11:27.267
She's programmed to do that
should certain conditions arise.
They have.

11:27.393 --> 11:30.395
[ Ripley ]
Like what?
It seems she has...

11:30.479 --> 11:32.689
intercepted a transmission
of unknown origin.

11:32.815 --> 11:36.025
She got us up to check it out.
A transmission?
Out here?

11:36.110 --> 11:38.862
Yeah.
What kind of a transmission?

11:38.946 --> 11:42.574
Acoustical beacon.
It repeats at intervals
of 12 seconds.

11:42.700 --> 11:44.576
S.O.S.?
I don't know.

11:44.660 --> 11:46.578
Human?

11:46.704 --> 11:49.539
Unknown.
[ Brett ]
Well, so what?

11:49.623 --> 11:51.749
[ Kane ]
We are obligated
under section eight-

11:51.834 --> 11:54.127
I hate to bring this up,
but, uh,

11:54.211 --> 11:56.546
this is a commercial ship,
not a rescue ship.

11:56.672 --> 12:00.091
Right.
And it's not in my contract
to do this kind of duty.

12:00.217 --> 12:04.095
And what about the money?
If you wanna give me some money,
I'll be happy to oblige.

12:04.221 --> 12:06.514
The man's right.
Let's go over
the bonus situation.

12:06.599 --> 12:10.518
- I'm sorry. Can I say something?
- Let's talk about the bonus more.

12:10.603 --> 12:13.229
There is a clause
in the contract
which specifically states...

12:13.314 --> 12:16.482
any systematized transmission
indicating a possible
intelligent origin...

12:16.609 --> 12:18.234
must be investigated.
I don't wanna hear it.

12:18.360 --> 12:20.528
We don't know
if it's intelligent.
I wanna go home and party.

12:20.613 --> 12:22.906
Parker, will you
just listen to the man?

12:25.117 --> 12:29.621
On penalty of
total forfeiture of shares.
No money.

12:30.998 --> 12:32.582
You got that?

12:32.666 --> 12:36.419
- [ Chuckling ]
Well, yeah.
- All right, we're going in.

12:36.503 --> 12:38.421
Yeah.
We're goin' in,
aren't we?

12:45.429 --> 12:47.096
[ Clears Throat ]
Can we all hear that,
Lambert?

12:47.181 --> 12:49.140
[ Beeping ]

12:55.439 --> 13:00.443
[ Electronic Pulsing ]

13:06.951 --> 13:09.827
[ Pulsing Continues ]

13:09.912 --> 13:11.871
[ Scoffs ]
Good God.

13:11.956 --> 13:14.332
Doesn't sound like
any radio signal
I've heard.

13:14.458 --> 13:16.626
Maybe it's a voice.
Well, we'll soon know.

13:16.710 --> 13:18.795
Can you hone in
on that?

13:19.922 --> 13:22.632
What was the, uh,
position?

13:22.716 --> 13:26.511
6550-99.

13:26.595 --> 13:28.721
[ Beeping ]

13:28.806 --> 13:31.224
[ Clacking ]

13:31.308 --> 13:34.185
[ Beeping ]
All right.
It found the quadrant.

13:34.270 --> 13:38.106
Ascension: six minutes,
20 seconds.

13:38.190 --> 13:42.777
Declination: 39 degrees,
two seconds.

13:42.861 --> 13:45.029
Okay. Put that
on the screen for me.

13:49.576 --> 13:51.411
[ Lambert ]
All right.
Well, that's it.

13:51.495 --> 13:54.914
It's a planetoid.
1200 kilometers.

13:54.999 --> 13:57.542
It's tiny.
Any rotation?

13:57.626 --> 13:59.919
[ Beeping ]

14:00.004 --> 14:02.422
[ Lambert ]
About two hours.

14:02.506 --> 14:04.841
What about gravity?

14:04.925 --> 14:07.302
Point eight-six.

14:09.596 --> 14:11.723
You can walk on it.

14:21.191 --> 14:24.819
[ Lambert Over Radio ]
Approaching orbital apogee.

14:24.903 --> 14:27.822
Mark 12, 11-

14:27.906 --> 14:30.325
Equatorial orbit nailed.

14:30.409 --> 14:33.703
[ Lambert ]
Nine, eight seconds
on descent.

14:33.787 --> 14:36.956
[ Kane ] Grids energized.
Fields focused.
Five. Four-

14:37.041 --> 14:40.251
[ Dallas, Indistinct ]

14:45.424 --> 14:48.468
- D.O.R.'s on line.
- How's the status on the lifters?

14:48.552 --> 14:51.095
Give me an A.C.
pressure reading.

14:57.603 --> 15:00.396
Forty-eight seconds
and counting.

15:00.481 --> 15:03.024
[ Ripley Over Radio ]
SR-1stable.

15:03.108 --> 15:05.610
Prepare to disengage
from platform.

15:05.694 --> 15:10.490
[ Lambert ]
Mark, 20 seconds.
Eighteen, 17-

15:10.574 --> 15:14.869
Twelve, 11, 10,

15:14.953 --> 15:17.538
nine, eight, seven,

15:17.623 --> 15:21.334
six, five, four,

15:21.418 --> 15:24.879
three, two, one, lock.

15:24.963 --> 15:26.798
Disengage.

15:31.929 --> 15:34.263
[ Ripley ]
Umbilicus clear.

15:38.435 --> 15:41.687
Money's safe.
Let's take her down.

15:43.649 --> 15:48.528
[ Parker ]
Nine, eight, seven-

15:48.612 --> 15:51.406
[ Kane ]
Roll 92 degrees port yaw.

15:51.490 --> 15:53.408
[ Ripley ]
Prime to port.

16:14.221 --> 16:17.056
[ Ripley ]
Prime ventral.
Prime dorsal.

16:17.141 --> 16:18.599
[ Kane ]
Down a degree.

16:23.355 --> 16:24.272
[ Lambert ]
39,000 meters.

16:25.691 --> 16:27.942
[ Dallas Over Radio,
Indistinct ]

16:32.030 --> 16:35.366
[ Ripley ]
Turbulence.

16:35.450 --> 16:37.702
[ Voices Over Radio
Continue ]

16:42.207 --> 16:45.459
Locked and floating.
You can drop us anytime now.
We'll catch you.

16:45.544 --> 16:50.381
Inertial damping's going off.
Hold on, people.
There's gonna be a little bump.

16:54.803 --> 16:56.804
[ Metal Creaking Loudly ]

16:56.889 --> 16:59.307
What the hell was that?

16:59.391 --> 17:01.851
Pressure drop in intake three.
Must've lost a shield.

17:01.935 --> 17:03.686
Let's go with it.

17:04.980 --> 17:07.148
[ Voices Over Radio
Continue ]

17:10.068 --> 17:13.571
[ Grunts ]
Dropping off now.

17:15.908 --> 17:17.909
Still dropping.

17:19.620 --> 17:21.579
Here we are.
We've got it.

17:21.663 --> 17:24.498
Take her down.

17:30.422 --> 17:32.548
Navigation lights on.

17:40.140 --> 17:44.185
[ Ash ]
We've got 5-3 still out.
No problem. Just down 11%.

17:44.269 --> 17:46.854
Grid status okay.

18:05.958 --> 18:07.875
[ Lambert ]
Nine,

18:07.960 --> 18:11.379
eight, seven, six,

18:11.463 --> 18:15.549
five, four, three,

18:15.634 --> 18:17.551
two, one.

18:17.636 --> 18:19.637
Kill drive engines.

18:30.899 --> 18:33.567
[ Alarm Blaring ]

18:38.490 --> 18:40.408
What the hell happened?

18:40.534 --> 18:45.079
[ Alarm Blaring ]
Somebody give me
a straight answer!

18:45.163 --> 18:49.166
- Is the hull breached?
- I don't see anything.
We've still got pressure.

18:49.251 --> 18:52.837
- Hit the screen.
- Right.

18:52.921 --> 18:55.506
[ Wind Howling ]

18:59.845 --> 19:03.848
[ Parker Over Radio ]
Secondary load sharing unit...

19:03.932 --> 19:05.850
is out.

19:05.934 --> 19:09.061
Three to four cells
are gone.

19:11.523 --> 19:14.525
Is that it?
No, hold on.

19:14.609 --> 19:17.903
We can't fix it
out here anyway,
and we need to reroute...

19:18.030 --> 19:21.532
a couple of these ducts,
wouldn't you say, Brett?
Dry dock time.

19:21.616 --> 19:23.951
Dry dock.
Tell her we need to dry-dock.

19:24.036 --> 19:25.953
Look, we couldn't fix it
out here anyway.

19:26.038 --> 19:27.955
We gotta reroute
all these ducts,

19:28.040 --> 19:30.666
and in order to do that
we've got to dry-dock.

19:30.751 --> 19:33.002
[ Sighs ]
What else?

19:33.086 --> 19:35.004
[ Parker Over Radio ]
Some fragments kicked up,

19:35.088 --> 19:37.465
and we've got to
clean it all out
and repressurize it.

19:37.549 --> 19:39.925
[ Ripley Over Radio ]
How long before
we're functional?

19:40.052 --> 19:44.472
Look, what is- What-
It's 17 hours, tell her.

19:44.598 --> 19:47.391
At least 25 hours.
Yeah.

19:47.476 --> 19:49.852
[ Ripley ]
Get started on the floor panel.
I'll be right down.

19:49.936 --> 19:51.979
What the hell's
she comin' down here for?

19:52.064 --> 19:54.148
She better stay
the fuck out of my way,
I'll tell you that.

19:54.232 --> 19:56.901
I'd like to see
what she's gonna do
when she gets here.

19:58.070 --> 20:00.780
[ Wind Howling ]

20:06.953 --> 20:10.664
Any response yet?
[ Ash ]
No. Absolutely nothing.

20:10.749 --> 20:13.918
Except
the same transmission
every 12 seconds.

20:14.002 --> 20:16.003
All the other channels
are dead.

20:21.093 --> 20:24.095
[ Clicks Switch ]
Kick on the floods.

20:38.777 --> 20:42.613
We can't go anywhere
in this.
Mmm.

20:42.697 --> 20:44.990
Well, Mother says
the sun's coming up
in 20 minutes.

20:45.117 --> 20:48.452
How far are we from
the source of transmission?
Uh, northeast.

20:48.537 --> 20:50.955
Just under 2,000 meters.

20:51.039 --> 20:53.541
Walking distance?

20:53.625 --> 20:56.168
[ Laughs ]
Well-

20:56.294 --> 20:59.422
Can you give me
an atmospheric?
Yes.

21:02.467 --> 21:04.468
[ Ash ]
Oh.

21:05.804 --> 21:07.888
It's almost primordial.

21:07.973 --> 21:09.974
There's inert nitrogen,

21:10.058 --> 21:12.726
high concentration
of carbon dioxide crystals,
methane.

21:12.811 --> 21:14.728
I'm working on
the trace elements.

21:14.813 --> 21:16.939
Anything else?
Yes.

21:17.023 --> 21:18.941
It's...

21:19.025 --> 21:21.402
rock, lava base,

21:21.486 --> 21:23.404
and deep cold.

21:23.488 --> 21:27.408
Well below the line.
Mm-hmm.

21:27.492 --> 21:30.161
[ Kane ]
I'll volunteer to be in
the first group to go out.

21:30.245 --> 21:32.997
[ Dallas ]
Yeah, that figures.

21:33.081 --> 21:35.875
You too, Lambert.

21:36.001 --> 21:39.503
Swell.
[ Dallas ] Better break
out the weapons.

22:09.075 --> 22:11.160
[ Wind Howling ]

22:53.328 --> 22:56.497
[ Lambert ]
I can't see a goddamn thing.

22:57.999 --> 23:00.000
[ Dallas ]
Ash, are you receiving?

23:00.085 --> 23:02.711
[ Voices Over Radio,
Indistinct ]

23:02.796 --> 23:04.713
[ Mouths Words ]

23:04.798 --> 23:07.091
[ Ash ]
Good contact on my board.

23:07.175 --> 23:11.428
[ Dallas Over Monitor ]
Clear and free.
Keep the line open. Let's go.

23:25.777 --> 23:28.612
Hey, Ripley.

23:28.697 --> 23:30.781
Hey, Ripley,
I wanna ask you a question.

23:33.159 --> 23:35.953
If they find what they're
lookin' for out there, does
that mean we get full shares?

23:36.037 --> 23:40.291
Don't worry, Parker.
You'll get whatever's
coming to you.

23:40.375 --> 23:42.918
Look, I'm not gonna do
any more work...

23:43.003 --> 23:45.921
till we get this
straightened out.
Brett,

23:46.047 --> 23:49.633
you're guaranteed by law
to get a share.
[ Parker ] What?

23:49.718 --> 23:52.886
- Why don't you just fuck off.
- What?

23:52.971 --> 23:55.389
[ Brett ]
What'd you say, Rip?

23:55.473 --> 23:59.143
If you have any trouble,
I'll be on the bridge.

24:00.562 --> 24:03.272
[ Parker ]
Hey, Ripley, come back here!

24:05.025 --> 24:08.110
[ Chuckling ]

24:08.236 --> 24:11.238
Son of a bitch.
What's the matter?

24:21.249 --> 24:23.959
[ Lambert ]
Can't see a goddamn thing.

24:24.044 --> 24:26.795
[ Kane ]
Quit griping.
I like griping.

24:26.880 --> 24:28.922
[ Dallas ]
Come on. Knock it off.

24:46.149 --> 24:48.108
[ Clacking ]

25:34.030 --> 25:36.824
[ Respirators Hissing ]

25:52.507 --> 25:54.925
Ash,
can you see this?

25:55.009 --> 25:57.219
Yes, I can.

26:00.348 --> 26:02.307
I've never seen
anything like it.

26:11.276 --> 26:13.736
[ Dallas ]
Very bizarre.

26:17.031 --> 26:19.074
[ Kane ]
You said it.

26:27.751 --> 26:30.127
[ Dallas ]
All right.

26:30.211 --> 26:32.713
Moving on to second...
position.

26:32.797 --> 26:35.424
[ Lambert ]
What is it?

26:37.510 --> 26:39.219
Let's get out of here.

26:39.304 --> 26:41.972
[ Kane ]
We've got this far.
We must go on.

26:42.056 --> 26:44.016
We have to go on.

26:47.270 --> 26:50.939
Will you say that again?
Shit.

26:52.400 --> 26:56.195
[ Dallas ]
Ash, as you can see,
it's kind of hard to describe.

26:56.279 --> 26:58.989
I'm going back to the console.

27:05.079 --> 27:07.956
[ Voices Continue Over Monitor,
Distorted ]

27:13.880 --> 27:16.131
[ Dallas, Faint ]
Seems to be solid.

27:16.216 --> 27:18.801
To walk-
You can on it.

27:26.100 --> 27:29.770
[ Dallas Continues,
Voice Distorted ]

27:40.824 --> 27:43.992
[ Dallas Continues,
Indistinct ]

27:45.745 --> 27:48.789
Dallas?

27:51.209 --> 27:53.710
[ Respirators Hissing ]

28:40.383 --> 28:42.593
Come on down here.
Something different down here.

28:44.053 --> 28:46.471
I don't know
what it is, but-

28:46.556 --> 28:49.933
See if we can get up that wall.
If we can get up that wall,
we can find out.

29:55.959 --> 29:57.960
Amazing.

29:58.044 --> 30:00.712
[ Dallas ]
Alien life-form.

30:02.465 --> 30:05.175
Looks like it's been dead
a long time.

30:05.259 --> 30:08.178
Fossilized.

30:08.262 --> 30:11.348
Looks like it's grown
out of the chair.

30:21.734 --> 30:23.860
Bones are bent outward,

30:23.945 --> 30:26.989
like he exploded from inside.

30:28.908 --> 30:31.743
[ Lambert ]
Wonder what happened
to the rest of the crew.

30:35.623 --> 30:39.209
Let's get the hell out of here.

30:50.847 --> 30:53.348
Hey, Dallas, Lambert,
come on over here.

30:57.103 --> 30:59.104
Come on.

31:03.109 --> 31:06.153
What do you got?
See what you make of this.

31:13.661 --> 31:15.579
[ Clicks Switch ]
Ash.

31:15.663 --> 31:19.082
That transmission-
Mother's deciphered part of it.

31:19.167 --> 31:21.626
It doesn't look like an S.O.S.
What is it, then?

31:21.711 --> 31:25.047
Well, I-
It looks like a warning.

31:25.131 --> 31:27.716
I'm gonna go out after them.
What's the point?

31:30.678 --> 31:33.805
I mean, by the time
it takes to get there,
you'll-

31:33.890 --> 31:36.349
they'll know if it's
a warning or not, yes?

31:36.434 --> 31:38.393
[ Clicks Switch ]

31:39.854 --> 31:42.064
[ Exhales Deeply ]

32:03.419 --> 32:05.462
[ Dallas ]
You okay down there?

32:09.759 --> 32:12.761
Can you see anything?
Uh... a cave.

32:14.013 --> 32:16.973
A ca- A cave of some sort.
But l-

32:19.143 --> 32:21.937
Well, I don't know,
but it's like
the goddamn tropics in here.

32:24.273 --> 32:27.400
What the hell is this?

32:54.971 --> 32:57.931
The cave is
completely enclosed,

32:58.015 --> 33:00.392
and it's full of...

33:00.476 --> 33:04.312
leathery objects,
like eggs or something.

33:06.816 --> 33:09.317
[ High-pitched Humming ]

33:22.123 --> 33:24.583
There's a layer of mist...
[ High-pitched Tone ]

33:24.667 --> 33:28.712
just covering the eggs
that reacts when broken.

33:31.883 --> 33:34.843
[ Dallas Over Radio ]
Kane? You all right?

33:34.927 --> 33:37.470
I'm okay.
All right.

33:39.682 --> 33:41.850
I'm okay.
I just slipped.

34:02.246 --> 34:04.956
Appears to be
completely sealed.

34:11.923 --> 34:13.715
[ Hisses ]

34:39.909 --> 34:42.202
Wait a minute.
There's movement.

34:43.996 --> 34:47.749
It seems to have life.
Organic life.

35:11.899 --> 35:13.733
[ Screeching ]

35:15.152 --> 35:17.487
[ Wind Howling ]

35:39.427 --> 35:41.136
[ Computer Clacking ]

35:52.189 --> 35:54.607
[ Dallas Over Radio ]
You there, Ripley?
I'm right here.

35:58.612 --> 36:01.156
[ Beeping ]

36:01.282 --> 36:04.200
Okay, Ripley, I'm at
the inner lock hatch now.
Right.

36:14.045 --> 36:16.796
Ripley.
We're clean. Let us in.
Right here.

36:16.881 --> 36:19.632
- What happened to Kane?
- Something has
attached itself to him.

36:19.717 --> 36:23.261
- We have to get him
to the infirmary right away.
- What kind of thing?

36:23.387 --> 36:25.638
I need a clear definition.
An organism.
Open the hatch.

36:25.723 --> 36:28.141
Wait a minute.
If we let it in,
the ship could be infected.

36:28.225 --> 36:32.020
You know
the quarantine procedure-
24 hours for decontamination.

36:32.104 --> 36:33.980
He could die in 24 hours.
Open the hatch.

36:34.065 --> 36:36.900
Listen to me.
If we break quarantine,
we could all die.

36:36.984 --> 36:41.363
Look, would you open
the goddamn hatch?
We have to get him inside.

36:42.740 --> 36:44.908
No. I can't do that.

36:44.992 --> 36:47.410
And if you
were in my position,
you'd do the same.

36:47.495 --> 36:49.371
Ripley, this is an order.
Open that hatch right now.

36:49.497 --> 36:51.373
Do you hear me?
Yes.

36:51.457 --> 36:53.500
Ripley, this is an order!
Do you hear me?

36:53.584 --> 36:57.379
Yes, I read you.
The answer is negative.

36:59.465 --> 37:01.424
Inner hatch opened.

37:02.426 --> 37:04.677
[ Whirring ]

37:28.119 --> 37:31.121
My God.

37:41.257 --> 37:43.341
What the hell is that?

37:44.635 --> 37:48.012
Jesus Christ.

37:49.974 --> 37:52.267
What is that, man?

37:54.061 --> 37:56.396
Hey, how the hell
is he breathing?

37:56.480 --> 37:58.398
Is he still alive
or what?

37:58.482 --> 38:01.442
Why don't
you guys
freeze him?

38:01.527 --> 38:03.528
How come
they don't
freeze him?

38:03.612 --> 38:05.572
What's going on
in there?

38:05.656 --> 38:07.991
What the fuck
is going on?
You bitch!

38:08.075 --> 38:10.535
Jesus Christ!
Hey! Hey!

38:10.619 --> 38:12.871
You would've
left us out there.
Break it up.

38:12.955 --> 38:17.458
[ Dallas ]
Ripley, when I give an order,
I expect to be obeyed.

38:17.543 --> 38:21.045
Even if it's
against the law?
You're goddamn right!

38:21.130 --> 38:23.923
Maybe she has a point.
Who the hell knows what that thing is.

38:24.008 --> 38:26.801
How are we gonna
get that off him?

38:26.927 --> 38:30.346
How are we gonna
get it off?
I'm gonna get some instruments.

38:34.393 --> 38:36.311
My God.

38:38.814 --> 38:42.567
Right.
I'll make an incision here.

38:42.693 --> 38:48.114
Try and remove
one of the digitals from-
You're gonna do what?

38:48.199 --> 38:51.284
Finger. I'm gonna try
and get his finger off.
Just a minute.

38:51.368 --> 38:53.912
[ Continues, Indistinct ]

38:56.582 --> 39:00.210
No, that's not- It's tearing
his scalp.
I know!

39:00.294 --> 39:04.589
It's not coming off
without tearing his face
off with it.

39:04.673 --> 39:06.507
We'll have to take
a look at him inside.
Right.

39:10.054 --> 39:12.805
How come
they don't freeze him?

39:12.890 --> 39:15.808
[ Parker Shouting ]
How come you guys
don't freeze him?

39:31.450 --> 39:33.910
All right, you can
take your mask off.

39:52.429 --> 39:58.351
- What's it got down his throat?
- I would suggest
it's feeding him oxygen.

39:58.435 --> 40:02.939
Paralyzes him,
puts him in a coma,
then keeps him alive.

40:03.023 --> 40:05.858
Now what the hell is that?

40:05.985 --> 40:07.902
We gotta
get it off of him.
Just a minute.

40:07.987 --> 40:09.904
Just a minute.

40:09.989 --> 40:12.448
I mean,
let's not be too hasty.

40:12.533 --> 40:14.701
We don't know anything
about...

40:14.785 --> 40:16.744
it.

40:16.829 --> 40:20.039
Now, we're assuming
it's feeding him oxygen.
If we remove it,

40:21.292 --> 40:23.293
it could kill him.

40:25.879 --> 40:28.047
I'm willing to take that chance.
Let's cut it off him now.

40:28.173 --> 40:31.926
You'll take responsibility?
Yes, I'll take responsibility.
Get him out of there.

40:33.637 --> 40:35.763
[ Dallas ]
Where do you wanna do this?

40:35.848 --> 40:39.017
We'll make an incision
just below the knuckle there.

40:39.143 --> 40:40.768
Right here.
Stand by.

40:44.732 --> 40:47.025
[ Whirring ]

40:49.570 --> 40:51.571
[ Ash ]
Good God!

40:54.992 --> 40:58.286
[ Dallas ]
That crap's gonna
eat through the hull.

41:00.205 --> 41:02.498
That thing's gonna eat
through the goddamn hull.
Come on!

41:02.583 --> 41:05.126
What's going on?

41:05.210 --> 41:07.211
This way.

41:15.346 --> 41:17.430
Next deck.

41:33.739 --> 41:36.866
- [ Sizzling ]
- [ Parker ]
There it is.

41:38.577 --> 41:40.536
Don't get under it!
Don't get under it.

41:46.377 --> 41:48.378
Looks like it's stopping.

41:51.256 --> 41:53.174
Take a look at this,
man.
Yeah.

41:53.258 --> 41:56.803
Brett, give me-
What do you got, a pen there?
Give it to me, quick.

41:56.887 --> 41:59.055
Come on! Come on!

42:03.435 --> 42:05.395
[ Brett ]
Don't get any on your arm.

42:12.403 --> 42:15.405
It stopped.

42:15.489 --> 42:19.534
Don't see anything
like that except, uh,
molecular acid.

42:19.618 --> 42:22.703
It must be using it
for blood.

42:22.788 --> 42:24.705
It's got a wonderful
defense mechanism.

42:24.790 --> 42:26.999
You don't dare kill it.

42:27.084 --> 42:28.960
What about Kane?

42:30.921 --> 42:34.382
- Here's your pen back.
- [ Brett ]
What do we do now?

42:34.466 --> 42:37.593
Leave Kane to Ash.
You get back to work.

42:39.805 --> 42:41.722
Well, what-

42:41.807 --> 42:44.809
[ Electrical Crackling ]

42:50.107 --> 42:52.942
Okay.

42:53.068 --> 42:55.945
Try it.
[ Motor Cranking ]

42:59.992 --> 43:01.993
Damn it.
I thought sure
that was it.

43:02.119 --> 43:05.371
Try it again.
[ Cranking ]

43:05.456 --> 43:08.082
I feel like I've been
in this place a month.

43:09.543 --> 43:12.128
We shouldn't have
landed in this place
in the first place.

43:13.797 --> 43:18.050
Shouldn't have landed
on this damn ball,
I know that.

43:18.135 --> 43:21.888
Well, the sooner we patch this
thing up and get out of here,
the sooner we can go home.

43:21.972 --> 43:23.306
This place
gives me the creeps.

44:27.996 --> 44:30.540
[ Ripley ]
That's amazing. What is it?

44:32.084 --> 44:35.294
Ah, yes, it is.
Um-

44:35.379 --> 44:37.505
I don't know yet.

44:40.300 --> 44:43.177
[ Coughs ]
Did you want something?

44:43.262 --> 44:45.555
Yes. I, uh-

44:47.349 --> 44:50.268
I'd like to have a little talk.
How's, uh- How's Kane?

44:50.352 --> 44:52.937
He's holding.
No changes.

44:53.021 --> 44:57.650
And, uh,
our guest?

44:57.776 --> 45:00.695
Well-
Hmm?

45:00.779 --> 45:02.655
Well, as I said,
I'm still...

45:02.739 --> 45:04.699
collating, actually,
but, uh,

45:04.783 --> 45:08.828
I have confirmed
that he's got an outer layer
of protein polysaccharides.

45:10.581 --> 45:12.873
He has a funny habit
of shedding his cells...

45:12.958 --> 45:16.794
and replacing them with...
polarized silicon,

45:16.878 --> 45:19.005
which gives him
a prolonged resistance...

45:19.089 --> 45:23.009
to adverse
environmental conditions.

45:23.135 --> 45:25.136
Is that enough for you?
That's plenty.

45:25.262 --> 45:28.514
What does it mean?
Please don't do that.
Thank you.

45:28.599 --> 45:31.642
I'm sorry.

45:31.727 --> 45:33.644
Well, it's
an interesting combination
of elements,

45:33.729 --> 45:38.274
making him
a tough little son of a bitch.

45:38.358 --> 45:40.735
And you let him in.

45:40.819 --> 45:43.195
I was obeying
a direct order, remember?

45:43.280 --> 45:47.366
Ash, when Dallas and Kane
are off the ship,

45:47.451 --> 45:49.535
I'm senior officer.

45:49.620 --> 45:52.496
Oh, yes. I forgot.

45:52.581 --> 45:56.000
You also forgot
the science division's
basic quarantine law.

45:56.126 --> 45:58.294
No, that I didn't forget.
Oh, I see.

45:58.378 --> 46:01.047
You just broke it.
Huh?

46:01.131 --> 46:04.759
Look, what would you
have done with Kane?
Hmm?

46:04.843 --> 46:08.137
You knew
his only chance of survival
was to get him in here.

46:08.221 --> 46:10.640
Unfortunately,
by breaking quarantine,

46:10.724 --> 46:12.683
you risk everybody's life.

46:12.768 --> 46:15.853
Maybe I should've
left him outside.

46:15.937 --> 46:19.774
Maybe I've jeopardized
the rest of us, but it was
a risk I was willing to take.

46:19.858 --> 46:22.026
That's a pretty big risk...

46:22.110 --> 46:24.028
for a science officer.

46:24.112 --> 46:27.490
It's, uh, not exactly
out of the manual, is it?

46:28.909 --> 46:32.328
I do take my responsibilities
as seriously as you, you know.

46:33.497 --> 46:35.414
You do your job...

46:35.499 --> 46:37.625
and let me do mine, yes?

46:50.639 --> 46:56.477
[ Wind Swirling ]
dd [ Classical ]

46:56.603 --> 47:00.940
[ Ripley ]
Where's Dallas?
[ Ash ] In the shuttle.

47:01.066 --> 47:03.567
dd [ Continues ]
[ Beep ]

47:03.652 --> 47:05.903
[ Clicks Switch ]

47:06.029 --> 47:08.572
Dallas.
[ Ash ] I think you should
have a look at Kane.

47:08.699 --> 47:12.702
Why?
Something's happened.

47:12.828 --> 47:15.830
Serious?
lnteresting.

47:18.375 --> 47:20.292
[ Clicks Switch ]
dd [ Stops ]

47:20.377 --> 47:22.336
Ripley, meet me
in the infirmary right away.

47:26.466 --> 47:28.426
[ Ripley ]
Where is it?

47:28.510 --> 47:31.345
[ Ash ]
Well, I don't know. I mean,
we ought to try and find it.

47:31.430 --> 47:33.347
[ Dallas ]
Yeah, let's check it.

47:39.563 --> 47:42.189
[ Slow Breaths ]

48:00.000 --> 48:02.293
Dallas,
please be careful.

48:40.624 --> 48:43.250
[ Loud Crash ]
[ Gasps ]

48:43.335 --> 48:45.711
Sorry.

49:17.536 --> 49:21.747
No, not in the corner.
Psst. Have one of these.

49:23.333 --> 49:25.251
Just in case.

49:37.681 --> 49:41.183
Kane? Dallas?
[ Screams ]

49:45.313 --> 49:48.482
You okay?
I didn't see it.
Was it in the overhead?

49:48.608 --> 49:52.361
What? It was
up there somewhere.
My God.

49:52.487 --> 49:55.614
[ Dallas ]
Cover up the damn thing!
[ Ash ] Wait.

49:55.699 --> 49:58.200
That's alive!

49:58.285 --> 50:00.286
That's a reflex action.

50:02.205 --> 50:04.123
Well, we've gotta
have a look at this.

50:16.011 --> 50:18.178
Excuse me.

50:24.811 --> 50:27.563
[ Ash ] Seems dead enough.
[ Ripley ] Well, good.
Let's get rid of it.

50:29.107 --> 50:31.609
Ripley, for God's sake,

50:31.693 --> 50:35.112
this is the first time
that we've encountered
a species like this.

50:35.196 --> 50:37.740
It has to go back.
All sorts of tests
have to be made.

50:37.824 --> 50:40.284
Ash, are you kidding?
This thing bled acid.

50:40.368 --> 50:43.120
Who knows what it's
gonna do when it's dead.

50:43.204 --> 50:46.415
Think it's safe to assume
it isn't a zombie.

50:46.499 --> 50:49.168
Dallas, it has to go back.

50:49.252 --> 50:51.754
Well, I'd soon...

50:51.838 --> 50:54.298
as not burn it at the stake,
but you're the science officer.

50:54.424 --> 50:55.758
It's your decision, Ash.
Dallas.

50:57.177 --> 50:59.470
How come
I've got to change my mind?
The decision's been made.

50:59.554 --> 51:01.972
I'm not trying
to change your mind, Dallas.
I just want you to listen-

51:02.057 --> 51:03.974
Will you listen to-

51:04.059 --> 51:06.268
[ Groans ]

51:06.353 --> 51:08.604
Just tell me how
you can leave that kind
of decision to him.

51:08.688 --> 51:10.689
Look, I just run the ship.

51:10.774 --> 51:13.233
Anything that has to do
with the science division,
Ash has the final word.

51:13.360 --> 51:16.654
-How does that happen?
-It happens, my dear, because that's
what the company wants to happen.

51:16.738 --> 51:19.448
Since when is that
standard procedure?

51:19.532 --> 51:22.117
Standard procedure
is to do what the hell
they tell you to do.

51:22.243 --> 51:25.996
What's happening with
the repairs? How's it going?
They're pretty much finished now.

51:26.081 --> 51:27.998
Why the hell
didn't you tell me so?

51:28.083 --> 51:30.668
- Because there's still
some things left to do.
- Like what?

51:30.752 --> 51:33.128
Well, we're blind
on "B" and "C" decks.

51:33.254 --> 51:36.090
The reserve power
system's blown-
That's a bunch of horseshit.

51:36.216 --> 51:39.343
We can take off without that.
Yeah, we can.
You think that's a good idea?

51:39.427 --> 51:42.304
Look, I just wanna get
the hell out of here,
all right?

51:42.389 --> 51:45.015
[ Engines Roaring ]

52:06.496 --> 52:09.123
Dust in the intakes again.
Number two's overheating.

52:09.207 --> 52:11.500
Spit on it for two minutes,
would you, for Christ's sake?

52:13.002 --> 52:15.337
[ Ripley ]
We're hot.
We're getting hotter.

52:18.091 --> 52:21.719
Engine room,
red clip status?

52:21.845 --> 52:25.806
One kilometer on ascension.
[ Ripley ]
Engage artificial gravity.

52:25.890 --> 52:29.476
Engaged.
I'm altering the vector now.

52:33.815 --> 52:35.816
[ Dallas ]
Inhibit C.N.G. control.

52:38.903 --> 52:43.741
Struts retract.
[ Parker ]
Struts retracted.

52:43.825 --> 52:47.953
[ Lambert ]
Max stress to fifth overload.

52:48.037 --> 52:50.497
[ Dallas ]
Ease it back.

52:51.624 --> 52:53.667
[ Dallas ]
She's great. Beautiful.

53:05.138 --> 53:08.265
Walk in the park.
When we fix something,
we stay fixed.

53:08.349 --> 53:11.185
Don't we, Brett baby?
[ Brett ]
Right.

53:26.493 --> 53:28.452
[ Parker ]
What I think we should do
is just freeze him.

53:28.536 --> 53:30.788
If he's got a disease,
why don't we stop it
where it is?

53:30.872 --> 53:34.500
- He can always get to a doctor
when we get back home.
- Right.

53:34.584 --> 53:38.253
Whenever he says anything,
you say "right," Brett.
You know that?

53:38.379 --> 53:40.547
Right.
[ Sighs ]

53:40.632 --> 53:43.509
Parker, what do you think?
Your staffjust follows you
around, says "right."

53:43.593 --> 53:46.011
- Just like a regular parrot.
- Yeah. Shape up.

53:46.095 --> 53:49.097
- What are you,
some kind of parrot?
- Right.

53:49.182 --> 53:52.184
Come on. Knock it off!
Kane's gonna have to
go into quarantine.

53:52.268 --> 53:55.062
That's it.
Yes, and so will we.

53:55.146 --> 53:57.397
Well, how about
a little something
to lower your spirits?

53:57.482 --> 53:59.566
Thrill me,
will you, please?

53:59.651 --> 54:01.568
Well, according
to my calculations,

54:01.653 --> 54:03.570
based on time spent getting
to and from the planet-

54:03.696 --> 54:06.949
Just give me the short version.
How far to Earth?
Ten months.

54:07.033 --> 54:08.951
Oh, God.
Great.

54:09.077 --> 54:10.869
[ Monitor Buzzes ]
Yes.

54:10.954 --> 54:12.955
[ Ash ]
Dallas, I think
you should come and see Kane.

54:13.081 --> 54:15.123
Has his condition changed?
It's simpler if you'd just
come and see him.

54:15.208 --> 54:16.208
[ Ripley ]
We're on our way.

54:20.004 --> 54:22.673
Right.

54:22.757 --> 54:24.967
[ Laughter ]

54:25.051 --> 54:27.427
[ Lambert ]
How are you doing?

54:29.806 --> 54:32.474
[ Coughs ]
Thank you.
How you doin'?

54:32.559 --> 54:34.768
Um, terrific.
Next silly question.

54:34.853 --> 54:36.854
[ Laughing ]

54:38.356 --> 54:40.399
Oh, thank you.

54:42.443 --> 54:45.070
Do you remember anything
about the planet?

54:47.991 --> 54:50.409
What's the last thing
you do remember?

54:51.953 --> 54:54.162
Huh?
[ Sighs ]

54:57.333 --> 54:59.251
I remember some...

54:59.335 --> 55:02.004
horrible dream about...
smothering.

55:02.088 --> 55:03.881
And-

55:03.965 --> 55:06.466
And- Anyway,
where are we?

55:06.593 --> 55:08.927
Right here.
We're on our way home.

55:09.012 --> 55:11.096
Back to the old
freezerinos.

55:13.266 --> 55:15.434
Could I have something to eat
before we go back?

55:15.518 --> 55:17.352
I-I need something myself.

55:17.437 --> 55:21.064
Yeah, right.
One more meal before bedtime.
I'm buyin'.

55:21.190 --> 55:24.234
Hey, that's a break.
Bedtime.

55:24.319 --> 55:27.988
[ Chattering ]

55:32.702 --> 55:35.162
[ Chattering Continues ]

55:44.005 --> 55:46.548
The first thing
that I'm gonna do
when I get back...

55:46.633 --> 55:48.634
is to get some decent food.

55:48.718 --> 55:51.428
I can dig it, man.
Let me tell you, I've eaten
worse food than this,

55:51.554 --> 55:54.222
but then I've tasted better,
you know what I'm sayin'?
The other one over there.

55:54.307 --> 55:57.392
Well, you
pound down the stuff
like there's no tomorrow.

55:57.477 --> 56:00.771
I'd rather be eatin'
something else, but, uh,
right now I'm thinkin' food.

56:00.855 --> 56:04.775
[ Kane ]
Well, you should know.
You know what it's made of.

56:04.859 --> 56:07.903
No, man, I don't wanna talk
about what it's made of.

56:08.029 --> 56:09.988
I'm eatin' this just to-
[ Gagging ]

56:11.366 --> 56:13.241
What's the matter?

56:13.368 --> 56:15.577
The food ain't
that bad, baby.
What's wrong, Kane?

56:15.703 --> 56:17.621
[ Gagging, Retching ]
Are you choking?

56:17.705 --> 56:19.581
What's wrong?

56:21.376 --> 56:23.543
[ Coughing, Gasping ]
What? What?

56:23.628 --> 56:26.672
- This is serious.
- Kane, what's the matter?

56:26.798 --> 56:30.759
[ Gagging, Gasping ]
It's okay!

56:30.843 --> 56:34.471
Hold him down!
Hold him-

56:34.555 --> 56:36.682
[ Ash ]
Get the spoon in!

56:36.766 --> 56:40.352
[ Groaning ]
Damn it!

56:40.478 --> 56:42.729
Get it into his mouth!
I'm trying!

56:42.814 --> 56:44.731
[ Screaming ]

56:54.784 --> 56:57.577
[ Screams ]

56:57.662 --> 57:00.372
[ Agonized Grunts ]

57:08.673 --> 57:10.507
- [ Screeching ]
- [ Screaming ]

57:10.591 --> 57:14.469
[ Lambert ]
Oh, my God! Oh, God!

57:22.603 --> 57:24.646
No!
Don't touch it!
Don't touch it!

57:29.068 --> 57:29.276
[ Screeching ]

57:41.247 --> 57:43.373
[ Brett ]
Dallas?

57:43.499 --> 57:46.043
Dallas?
Yeah.

57:46.169 --> 57:50.005
Anything?
No. You?

57:50.089 --> 57:52.424
Nothing.

57:52.550 --> 57:55.135
You see anything?
No.

58:15.490 --> 58:18.325
[ Loud Clank ]
[ Dallas ]
Inner hatch sealed.

58:21.329 --> 58:24.372
Anybody wanna say anything?

59:00.868 --> 59:04.329
This is just an ordinary prod,
like a cattle prod.

59:04.413 --> 59:06.331
It's got a portable battery.

59:06.415 --> 59:09.126
It's insulated
all the way here,
all the way up to here.

59:09.210 --> 59:12.170
Just make damn sure
nobody puts their hand
on the end of it.

59:15.716 --> 59:17.634
It shouldn't damage
the little bastard,

59:17.718 --> 59:20.220
unless its skin's
thinner than ours.

59:20.304 --> 59:24.474
But it will give him
a little incentive.

59:24.559 --> 59:26.560
Now we just have
to find it.

59:26.644 --> 59:30.480
I've taken care of that.
I've designed
this tracking device.

59:30.565 --> 59:34.985
You just set it
to search for
a moving object, like so.

59:35.069 --> 59:37.571
Hasn't got much of a range,
but when you get
within a certain distance,

59:37.655 --> 59:39.698
it'll start
to give off a signal.

59:39.782 --> 59:42.868
What's it key on?

59:42.952 --> 59:46.705
Micro changes
in air density.

59:46.789 --> 59:49.166
Give me a demo.

59:50.835 --> 59:54.504
[ Whirring ]
See?
Again.

59:54.589 --> 59:56.923
Got ya.

59:57.008 --> 01:00:00.510
Two teams.
Ash, Lambert and l.

01:00:00.595 --> 01:00:04.014
Ripley, you take
Parker and Brett.

01:00:04.098 --> 01:00:06.600
Now, anyone see this thing,
you catch it in the net...

01:00:06.684 --> 01:00:08.810
that Parker's holding
on his lap.

01:00:08.895 --> 01:00:11.813
Parker, I don't want
any heroics out of you,
all right?

01:00:11.898 --> 01:00:15.317
Catch it,
put it in the air lock,
get rid of it.

01:00:15.401 --> 01:00:17.277
Now, channels are open
on all decks.

01:00:17.361 --> 01:00:21.489
I want you to communicate,
keep in touch
at all times, all right?

01:00:21.574 --> 01:00:23.575
Let's go.

01:00:28.122 --> 01:00:29.789
I thought
you fixed 12 module.

01:00:29.874 --> 01:00:32.042
[ Brett ]
We did.

01:00:32.126 --> 01:00:34.169
I don't
understand it.

01:00:36.297 --> 01:00:38.590
[ Parker ]
The circuits
must have burned out.

01:00:51.395 --> 01:00:54.230
What do we got here?
Damn it! Hold your light
over here, would you?

01:00:54.315 --> 01:00:56.232
Yeah, that's it.

01:00:56.317 --> 01:01:00.278
I don't know if this
is gonna work.

01:01:00.363 --> 01:01:02.989
If I could just put this-
put this in there.

01:01:03.074 --> 01:01:05.825
Right.
Oh, damn it.

01:01:09.038 --> 01:01:11.498
Check
the insulation.

01:01:11.582 --> 01:01:13.500
Oh, shit!

01:01:25.012 --> 01:01:28.890
[ Tracking Device Whirring ]

01:01:35.856 --> 01:01:39.234
Steady.
According to this,
it's within five meters.

01:01:40.444 --> 01:01:42.529
[ Indistinct Whispering ]

01:01:44.198 --> 01:01:47.033
[ Ripley ]
Micro changes
in air density, my ass.

01:01:47.118 --> 01:01:49.244
[ Tracking Device Beeping ]

01:01:52.748 --> 01:01:55.208
It's within five meters.

01:01:55.292 --> 01:01:57.127
[ Parker ]
Be careful.

01:02:04.301 --> 01:02:06.594
[ Beeping Continues ]

01:02:06.721 --> 01:02:09.639
[ Ripley ] Christ.
[ Parker ] Don't do that.
Don't creep up on me with that thing.

01:02:09.724 --> 01:02:12.517
[ Ripley ]
You guys, stick together.

01:02:19.025 --> 01:02:23.194
[ Tracker Twittering ]

01:02:27.992 --> 01:02:31.703
Don't fail me now.
[ Parker ]
What?

01:02:31.829 --> 01:02:33.997
What is it?
Parker, Brett,
it's in this locker!

01:02:34.081 --> 01:02:35.999
Where?

01:02:36.083 --> 01:02:38.084
[ Brett ]
Here, take this.

01:02:38.169 --> 01:02:40.587
Get over there
and get the net.

01:02:40.713 --> 01:02:43.298
Get it?
I got it. I got it.
I got it.

01:02:43.382 --> 01:02:45.967
Wait a minute.
Wait a minute.

01:02:47.720 --> 01:02:50.764
All right, Parker.
When I say.

01:02:51.766 --> 01:02:54.350
All right. Now.

01:02:54.435 --> 01:02:56.436
Easy.

01:02:58.272 --> 01:03:00.023
[ Hissing ]

01:03:00.107 --> 01:03:02.734
- [ All Chattering ]
- Wait! Don't let him go!

01:03:02.818 --> 01:03:05.028
What the hell
are you doing, man?

01:03:05.112 --> 01:03:07.030
It's the cat.

01:03:07.114 --> 01:03:09.949
[ Laughing ]

01:03:13.496 --> 01:03:16.372
Hey, look, now.
We had to bag it, man.

01:03:16.457 --> 01:03:19.667
Now we might
pick it up
on the tracker again.

01:03:19.794 --> 01:03:22.045
I'll- I'll- I'll-
Go and get it, man.

01:03:23.047 --> 01:03:24.964
All right.
You get him.
We'll go on.

01:03:27.968 --> 01:03:30.053
[ Sighs ]
[ Scoffs ]

01:03:36.477 --> 01:03:38.895
Here, kitty!

01:03:38.979 --> 01:03:41.356
Here, kitty, kitty!

01:03:41.440 --> 01:03:44.067
Enough of that
kitty crap.

01:03:44.151 --> 01:03:48.071
Jones.

01:03:48.155 --> 01:03:50.073
Jonesy?

01:03:50.157 --> 01:03:52.158
Here, Jonesy.

01:03:53.828 --> 01:03:57.288
[ Meowing ]
[ Cat Mewing ]

01:03:59.917 --> 01:04:01.835
Jonesy?

01:04:07.007 --> 01:04:09.342
Here, kitty, kitty, kitty.

01:04:10.803 --> 01:04:12.804
[ Meowing ]

01:04:15.850 --> 01:04:18.226
Here, Jonesy.

01:04:30.030 --> 01:04:31.906
Jonesy?

01:04:31.991 --> 01:04:34.200
[ Faint Meowing ]

01:04:43.169 --> 01:04:45.336
Here, kitty, kitty.

01:04:52.970 --> 01:04:55.763
[ Meowing ]

01:05:22.791 --> 01:05:26.461
[ Footsteps Echoing ]

01:05:41.810 --> 01:05:44.979
[ Liquid Splashing ]

01:05:56.283 --> 01:05:59.077
[ Chains Clinking ]

01:06:12.549 --> 01:06:15.134
Kitty, kitty, kitty.

01:06:16.887 --> 01:06:19.222
Here, Jonesy.

01:06:19.306 --> 01:06:21.307
Jonesy.

01:06:23.560 --> 01:06:25.561
Kitty, kitty.

01:06:59.221 --> 01:07:01.431
Kitty, kitty, kitty.

01:07:05.144 --> 01:07:07.145
Jonesy?

01:07:14.153 --> 01:07:16.988
Hey. Hey.
Come on, Jonesy.

01:07:17.072 --> 01:07:19.365
Come on, baby.
That's a kitty.

01:07:19.450 --> 01:07:22.827
That's a kitty.
Come on, baby.

01:07:22.911 --> 01:07:25.705
- That's a kitty.
- [ Hisses ]

01:07:25.789 --> 01:07:29.667
Hey, hey.
I'm not gonna hurt you.

01:07:29.752 --> 01:07:31.753
Come on.

01:07:36.592 --> 01:07:38.968
[ Snarling ]

01:07:52.691 --> 01:07:55.026
[ Screaming ]

01:08:01.200 --> 01:08:03.117
Brett!

01:08:03.202 --> 01:08:05.536
[ Parker ]
Brett!

01:08:12.795 --> 01:08:15.380
Brett!

01:08:24.098 --> 01:08:26.974
Whatever it was, it was-
it was big and-

01:08:30.396 --> 01:08:32.688
You're sure it took him
into the air shaft?

01:08:32.773 --> 01:08:34.941
Disappeared into
one of the cooling ducts.

01:08:35.025 --> 01:08:37.360
No question, it's-
it's using the air ducts
to move around.

01:08:41.490 --> 01:08:43.658
Could he want
Brett alive?

01:08:44.993 --> 01:08:47.662
What?
Could Brett be alive?

01:08:47.746 --> 01:08:50.415
No. I mean,
I don't think so.

01:08:50.499 --> 01:08:54.419
Well, this air shaft may
work to our advantage.

01:08:54.503 --> 01:08:59.298
Here it leads up to
and comes out in
the main air lock.

01:08:59.383 --> 01:09:01.676
All right. There's only
one big opening
along the way.

01:09:01.760 --> 01:09:05.096
We can cover that up,
and then we...

01:09:05.180 --> 01:09:07.682
drive it into the air lock
and zap it
into outer space.

01:09:07.766 --> 01:09:10.143
This son of a bitch
is huge!

01:09:10.227 --> 01:09:13.604
- I mean, it's like
a man. It's big!
- Kane's son.

01:09:16.024 --> 01:09:18.484
Come on, Ash.
Science department
should be able to help us.

01:09:18.569 --> 01:09:20.945
What can we do
to drive it?

01:09:21.029 --> 01:09:23.322
Yes, well, it's adapted
remarkably well
to our atmosphere,

01:09:23.407 --> 01:09:25.491
considering its
nutritional requirements.

01:09:25.617 --> 01:09:28.161
- The only thing we don't
know about is temperature.
- Okay. What about temperature?

01:09:28.245 --> 01:09:30.955
- What happens
if we change it?
- Let's try it.

01:09:31.039 --> 01:09:34.333
I mean, most animals
retreat from fire. Yes?

01:09:34.418 --> 01:09:36.878
Fire, yeah.
Parker, can you rig...

01:09:36.962 --> 01:09:39.464
three or four
incinerator units?

01:09:39.548 --> 01:09:42.133
Give me about 20 minutes.
I'll do it.

01:09:42.217 --> 01:09:43.885
- Who gets to go
into the vent?
- I do.

01:09:46.597 --> 01:09:50.349
No.
You and Ash...

01:09:50.434 --> 01:09:52.602
take the main
air lock.

01:09:52.686 --> 01:09:56.481
Parker, Lambert,
you cover up that
maintenance opening, please.

01:09:56.565 --> 01:09:58.983
[ Lambert ]
Right.

01:10:03.030 --> 01:10:05.990
[ Beeping ]

01:10:28.222 --> 01:10:31.766
- [ Dallas ]
I'm at the first junction.
- Dallas, I'm right here.

01:10:31.850 --> 01:10:35.645
- Parker?
- Yeah?
- Lambert?

01:10:35.729 --> 01:10:38.022
We're in position.
I'm just trying to get
a reading here.

01:10:38.106 --> 01:10:40.858
- The air lock is open.
- Okay, Ripley.

01:10:40.943 --> 01:10:43.611
Ready.

01:10:52.955 --> 01:10:55.706
All right. I've got
a reading on you now.

01:10:55.791 --> 01:10:57.792
[ Tracker Beeping ]

01:11:11.807 --> 01:11:15.101
Uh, open the hatch
to the third junction.

01:11:17.688 --> 01:11:20.606
[ Beeping ]

01:11:30.576 --> 01:11:33.452
[ Beeping Continues ]
[ Dallas ]
Okay, I'm through.

01:11:33.579 --> 01:11:35.496
Ripley?
Yes.

01:11:35.581 --> 01:11:38.374
Close all the hatches
behind me.

01:11:38.458 --> 01:11:40.626
I'm moving on.

01:11:55.350 --> 01:11:57.560
[ Lambert ]
Dallas, hold it a minute.
I think I got it.

01:11:57.686 --> 01:12:02.315
Yes, I've got it.
[ Dallas ]
Where?

01:12:02.399 --> 01:12:06.152
[ Lambert ] It's somewhere around
the third junction.

01:12:06.236 --> 01:12:08.237
Okay, moving on.

01:12:27.591 --> 01:12:31.135
It is right around there.
Now, Dallas, you're gonna
have to be careful.

01:12:41.355 --> 01:12:46.484
All right.
I've reached...

01:12:46.568 --> 01:12:50.404
the third junction,
and I'm going down.

01:12:50.489 --> 01:12:54.033
[ Sensors Beeping ]

01:12:56.244 --> 01:12:58.662
[ Beeping ]

01:13:07.506 --> 01:13:10.841
The hell's the matter
with that box?

01:13:10.926 --> 01:13:14.720
Dallas, you're gonna
have to hold your position
for a minute. I-

01:13:14.805 --> 01:13:16.847
I've lost the signal.

01:13:16.932 --> 01:13:19.850
What? You sure?

01:13:19.935 --> 01:13:24.021
Look around. Are you sure
it's not there? It's got to
be around there somewhere.

01:13:28.193 --> 01:13:32.071
[ Dallas ] Checked it out,
Lambert. You may be
getting interserence.

01:13:32.155 --> 01:13:33.989
[ Lambert ] Dallas, are you
sure there's no sign of it?

01:13:34.074 --> 01:13:38.786
I mean, it is there.
It's gotta be around there.

01:13:40.497 --> 01:13:45.584
- Dallas?
- God, what is happening?

01:13:45.669 --> 01:13:48.462
All right.

01:13:52.467 --> 01:13:56.929
Uh, am I- am I clear, Lambert?
I want to get the hell
out of here.

01:13:57.013 --> 01:13:59.056
[ Beeping ]

01:13:59.141 --> 01:14:01.725
[ Lambert ]
Oh, God. It's moving
right towards you.

01:14:03.812 --> 01:14:05.646
Um-

01:14:09.901 --> 01:14:14.238
Move! Get out of there!
Behind you! Move!

01:14:14.322 --> 01:14:17.408
Dallas! Move, Dallas!
Move, Dallas!

01:14:17.492 --> 01:14:21.162
Get out!
[ Sobbing ]
Move!

01:14:21.246 --> 01:14:22.913
The other way!

01:14:22.998 --> 01:14:24.707
[ Screeching ]

01:14:24.833 --> 01:14:26.584
[ Shrill Feedback ]
Dallas?

01:14:26.710 --> 01:14:28.461
Oh, no.
Take it easy.

01:14:28.545 --> 01:14:30.671
[ Parker ]
Dallas?

01:14:36.178 --> 01:14:38.345
We found this laying there.

01:14:40.015 --> 01:14:42.266
No blood.

01:14:42.350 --> 01:14:45.769
No Dallas.
Nothing.

01:14:52.027 --> 01:14:54.487
How come I don't hear
nobody saying nothing?
I'm thinking.

01:14:57.574 --> 01:15:02.119
Unless somebody has got
a better idea,

01:15:02.204 --> 01:15:04.455
we'll proceed
with Dallas's plan.

01:15:04.539 --> 01:15:08.292
What? And end up
like the others?

01:15:08.376 --> 01:15:10.794
Ohh. No, you're
out of your mind.

01:15:10.879 --> 01:15:15.132
- Got a better idea?
- Yes. I say that we
abandon this ship.

01:15:15.217 --> 01:15:17.468
We get the shuttle
and just get the hell
out of here.

01:15:17.552 --> 01:15:20.513
We take our chances
and just hope that...

01:15:20.597 --> 01:15:22.473
somebody picks us up.
Lambert.

01:15:22.599 --> 01:15:26.310
The shuttle won't take four.
Then why don't we draw
straws and-

01:15:26.394 --> 01:15:29.480
I'm not drawin' any straws.
I'm for killing
that goddamn thing right now.

01:15:29.564 --> 01:15:31.607
[ Ripley ]
Okay.

01:15:31.733 --> 01:15:33.734
Well, let's talk about
killing it.
[ Parker Grumbling ]

01:15:33.818 --> 01:15:36.946
We know it's using
the air shafts- Will you
listen to me, Parker?

01:15:37.072 --> 01:15:39.865
Shut up!
Let's hear it.

01:15:39.950 --> 01:15:41.867
Let's hear it.

01:15:41.952 --> 01:15:45.162
It's using the air shafts.

01:15:45.288 --> 01:15:48.040
We don't know that.
That's the only way.

01:15:48.124 --> 01:15:51.210
We'll move in pairs.
We'll go step by step...

01:15:51.294 --> 01:15:54.213
and cut off
every bulkhead
and every vent...

01:15:54.297 --> 01:15:57.550
until we have it cornered,
and then we'll blow it
the fuck out into space.

01:15:57.634 --> 01:15:59.802
Is that acceptable
to you?

01:15:59.928 --> 01:16:05.015
If it means killing it,
it's acceptable to me.
Obviously it means killing it.

01:16:05.100 --> 01:16:06.892
But we have to
stick together.

01:16:08.270 --> 01:16:11.689
How are our weapons?
The weapons are fine.

01:16:11.815 --> 01:16:15.693
This one needs
refueling.
Will you get it, please?

01:16:15.819 --> 01:16:19.822
Ash, go with him.
No, no. I can
manage, Ash.

01:16:19.906 --> 01:16:21.907
Don't follow me.

01:16:25.453 --> 01:16:27.454
Ash?

01:16:28.748 --> 01:16:31.250
Any suggestions
from you or Mother?

01:16:33.169 --> 01:16:37.047
No, we're still
collating.

01:16:37.132 --> 01:16:39.383
[ Laughs ]
You're what?

01:16:39.467 --> 01:16:41.677
You're still collating?

01:16:41.761 --> 01:16:44.805
I find that
hard to believe.

01:16:46.850 --> 01:16:50.019
What would you like me to do?
Just what you've
been doing, Ash.

01:16:50.103 --> 01:16:53.063
Nothing.
I've got access
to Mother now,

01:16:53.148 --> 01:16:56.108
and I'll get
my own answers, thank you.

01:16:58.737 --> 01:17:01.280
All right.

01:17:12.792 --> 01:17:16.754
[ Clicking, Beeping ]

01:17:25.805 --> 01:17:28.432
[ Whirring ]

01:17:29.476 --> 01:17:47.660
[ Keyboard Beeping ]

01:18:39.170 --> 01:18:42.464
There is an explanation
for this, you know.

01:18:42.549 --> 01:18:46.552
Is there really?
I don't wanna hear
your goddamn explanation!

01:18:48.680 --> 01:18:51.849
[ Sobbing ]
I want- I want-

01:18:53.268 --> 01:18:57.479
[ Sobbing ]
I want- I w-

01:19:03.903 --> 01:19:07.030
Parker. Lambert?

01:19:15.248 --> 01:19:18.667
Ash, open the door.

01:19:28.303 --> 01:19:30.304
Ash-

01:19:34.225 --> 01:19:36.226
Will you open the door?

01:19:39.564 --> 01:19:41.064
Let me by, Ash.
[ Giggling ]

01:19:47.864 --> 01:19:49.656
[ Screams ]

01:20:12.514 --> 01:20:15.474
[ Jingling ]

01:20:17.227 --> 01:20:19.228
Yaah!
[ Groans ]

01:20:53.346 --> 01:20:55.764
[ Muffled Shouts ]

01:21:03.106 --> 01:21:05.607
The hell are you doing?

01:21:09.863 --> 01:21:12.823
[ Muffled Shouting Continues ]

01:21:12.907 --> 01:21:14.908
Aah!

01:21:23.459 --> 01:21:27.212
Get her up. Get her up.
Get her up. Get her up.
Get her up. Get her up.

01:21:27.297 --> 01:21:31.300
[ Chittering ]

01:21:38.600 --> 01:21:40.934
Android!
He's an android!

01:21:53.740 --> 01:21:55.657
[ Screeching ]

01:21:55.742 --> 01:21:57.743
Jesus!

01:22:00.955 --> 01:22:04.207
[ Parker ]
It's a robot.
Ash is a goddamn robot!

01:22:06.169 --> 01:22:08.378
God!

01:22:10.840 --> 01:22:14.509
[ Parker ]
Oh! Get off me- Oh!

01:22:14.594 --> 01:22:16.553
Holy shit!

01:22:16.638 --> 01:22:21.099
Help! Help me get
this fucking thing off!

01:22:21.184 --> 01:22:23.185
[ Screaming ]

01:22:24.979 --> 01:22:27.314
Aah!

01:22:28.775 --> 01:22:31.026
God! Jesus!
Oh, God! Oh, God!

01:22:35.740 --> 01:22:38.700
[ Parker ]
How come the company
sent us a goddamn robot?

01:22:38.785 --> 01:22:42.537
[ Ripley ] All I can think of is
they must've wanted the alien
for their weapons division.

01:22:42.622 --> 01:22:45.415
He's been protecting it
right along.

01:22:45.500 --> 01:22:47.751
Parker, will you
plug it in?

01:22:47.877 --> 01:22:52.756
[ Parker ] I don't know why-
Because he may know
how to kill it.

01:23:17.990 --> 01:23:20.492
[ Ripley ]
Ash, can you hear me?

01:23:23.663 --> 01:23:25.580
Ash?

01:23:32.714 --> 01:23:35.465
[ Distorted Voice ]
Yes, I can hear you.

01:23:39.929 --> 01:23:45.475
- What was your special order?
- You read it.
I thought it was clear.

01:23:45.560 --> 01:23:49.563
- What was it?
- Bring back life-form.

01:23:49.647 --> 01:23:54.317
Priority one. All other
priorities rescinded.

01:23:57.321 --> 01:24:02.033
The damn company!
What about our lives,
you son of a bitch?

01:24:02.118 --> 01:24:06.079
I repeat: All other priorities
are rescinded.

01:24:06.164 --> 01:24:08.540
[ Ripley ]
How do we kill it, Ash?

01:24:08.624 --> 01:24:12.043
There's got to be
a way of killing it.
How- How do we do it?

01:24:12.128 --> 01:24:14.921
You can't.

01:24:15.006 --> 01:24:20.510
-That's bullshit!
-You still don't understand what
you're dealing with, do you?

01:24:21.971 --> 01:24:24.473
A persect organism.

01:24:27.268 --> 01:24:30.896
Its structural persection
is matched only
by its hostility.

01:24:30.980 --> 01:24:33.190
You admire it.

01:24:37.278 --> 01:24:39.362
I admire its purity.

01:24:43.701 --> 01:24:45.619
A survivor...

01:24:47.705 --> 01:24:51.958
unclouded by conscience,

01:24:52.043 --> 01:24:55.712
remorse or delusions
of morality.

01:24:57.673 --> 01:25:00.342
[ Parker ]
Look, I- I've heard
enough of this,

01:25:00.426 --> 01:25:02.844
and I'm asking you
to pull the plug.

01:25:02.929 --> 01:25:06.264
